<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shining Path</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1969–</span> · Also known as Sendero Luminoso, Communist Party of Peru – Shining Path</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shining Path is a Maoist insurgent organisation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, founded around 1969 by the philosophy professor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abimael-guzman">Abimael Guzmán</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayacucho">Ayacucho</a>. It launched an armed struggle in 1980, and the conflict with the state cost some 70,000 lives by official estimates. The movement collapsed after Guzmán's capture in 1992, though small remnants survived in remote valleys.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shining-path.jpg" alt="Shining Path" width="320" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cesar David MP · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_PCP-Shining_Path.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
